WEBVTT

00:00.690 --> 00:02.980
The Pokémon Elections 720!

00:03.900 --> 00:07.170
These Pokémon Elections will determine the Pokémon that will be given away during the movie!

00:08.090 --> 00:11.550
We will be now start taking your votes via the data broadcast!

00:12.820 --> 00:16.290
Push the d-button on your remote control and vote for the Pokémon you want!

00:16.880 --> 00:18.850
All right, the anime starts now!

00:22.030 --> 00:31.840
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:35.580 --> 00:39.740
Satoshi and his friends are on their way towards Eisetsu City in order to get the eighth badge.

00:40.620 --> 00:43.760
Right now, they have stopped by a Pokémon Center in a town.

00:46.590 --> 00:50.060
Ahem. I will now present my own personal hypothesis...

00:50.460 --> 00:52.650
... as to what happens to Satoshi and Gekkouga!

00:54.410 --> 00:56.850
It is time for science to open up the future!

00:57.850 --> 00:59.260
Citronic Gear, on!

01:00.300 --> 01:01.240
Wow!

01:02.650 --> 01:03.630
The Citroid?

01:04.780 --> 01:06.050
So cute!

01:07.840 --> 01:10.750
This is the groundbreaking machine that will assist me.

01:11.130 --> 01:13.200
I call it the Citroid Mini.

01:13.460 --> 01:14.500
Wow!

01:15.850 --> 01:17.090
All right, Citroid Mini.

01:17.640 --> 01:19.630
Please reveal the results of the analysis.

01:22.960 --> 01:25.740
So far, Gekkouga has undergone a transformation three times.

01:28.160 --> 01:32.370
What we know is that that phenomenon occurs during battles.

01:33.180 --> 01:36.820
We also know that Gekkouga's appearance resembles Satoshi.

01:37.440 --> 01:43.230
That is, I believe, because the phenomenon seems to be heavily related to Satoshi and Gekkouga's psyche.

01:44.080 --> 01:45.100
Psyche?

01:45.730 --> 01:52.550
In other words, when the two of them feel the same way, their physical reactions might start to resemble each other as well.

01:53.180 --> 01:55.970
Hey, come to think of it... Gojika-san told us about this.

01:57.000 --> 01:59.220
This one will gain further power.

02:00.370 --> 02:01.660
However, this one's future...

02:02.300 --> 02:05.450
...is you two climbing up towards a future of new greatness...

02:06.350 --> 02:10.060
...that no one has ever seen before.

02:11.610 --> 02:15.480
Oh, of course! <i>This</i> is what Gojika-san's prediction was referring to!

02:15.760 --> 02:19.570
Gojika-san also said that Gekogashira wanted your love, Satoshi.

02:21.040 --> 02:25.070
However, what Keromatsu wanted was something deeper.

02:26.020 --> 02:27.460
I call this...

02:28.590 --> 02:29.660
...love.

02:30.460 --> 02:33.000
Could this be a factor in the transformation as well?

02:33.520 --> 02:37.080
Shota said that Pokémon and Trainers with a deep relationship act similar to each other.

02:37.570 --> 02:39.420
This might be something along those lines.

02:40.660 --> 02:41.600
Heh heh heh...

02:41.900 --> 02:45.390
Now then, let us try to verify my hypothesis right away!

02:49.300 --> 02:55.010
Satoshi and Alan!
Gekkouga VS Mega Lizardon Once Again!!

03:01.820 --> 03:03.020
What's this?

03:04.340 --> 03:05.660
Citronic Gear,

03:06.200 --> 03:06.830
on!

03:07.080 --> 03:08.520
Part two!

03:08.950 --> 03:11.740
I call this the Battle Pulse Measuring Instrument!

03:12.380 --> 03:13.580
"Battle Pulse"?

03:14.830 --> 03:20.170
It is a collection of data on things like your brain waves and heart rate during battle.

03:21.110 --> 03:27.000
The instrument will record when and where Gekkouga transforms and how Satoshi reacts when it happens.

03:28.000 --> 03:28.790
Wow...

03:29.180 --> 03:31.740
All right then, let's go all out, Gekkouga!

03:36.610 --> 03:37.830
Let us begin, then.

03:38.180 --> 03:39.920
Rentorar, Electric Terrain!

03:48.620 --> 03:50.480
We will not go easy on you, Satoshi!

03:50.920 --> 03:51.780
Bring it on!

03:52.200 --> 03:53.810
Gekkouga, Cut!

03:56.230 --> 03:57.340
Thunder Fang!

04:06.280 --> 04:07.170
Brute force, huh?

04:07.470 --> 04:08.900
We are not done yet!

04:08.900 --> 04:10.610
Rentorar, Wild Charge!

04:13.270 --> 04:14.210
Double Team!

04:26.310 --> 04:26.770
Now!

04:27.070 --> 04:27.810
Aerial Ace!

04:36.770 --> 04:37.700
So this is what you chose to go with.

04:38.180 --> 04:42.220
Amazing! Satoshi and Gekkouga are perfectly in sync!

04:51.750 --> 04:53.430
Welcome to the Pokémon Center.

05:08.640 --> 05:09.790
Time-out, time-out!

05:10.300 --> 05:11.610
It is taking a long time to transform, huh?

05:12.140 --> 05:13.980
I guess it doesn't happen every day.

05:15.180 --> 05:17.820
<i>We</i> don't know why it happens either, so...

05:18.180 --> 05:19.100
Right, Gekkouga?

05:21.320 --> 05:24.120
Could there be other factors involved...?

05:29.240 --> 05:31.830
You're always in the middle of a battle whenever I run into you.

05:32.620 --> 05:33.040
Alan!

05:34.110 --> 05:35.460
That's an interesting gadget you're wearing.

05:36.980 --> 05:37.380
Yeah.

05:38.080 --> 05:40.810
We were in the middle of examining that power Gekkouga has.

05:41.480 --> 05:43.570
But it doesn't look like it's working today.

05:43.880 --> 05:45.810
There must be some other factors involved.

05:46.400 --> 05:47.280
That's right!

05:47.700 --> 05:48.730
Let's battle, Alan!

05:49.730 --> 05:52.690
Oh, please do. I want to focus on the measuring.

05:54.240 --> 05:56.940
Yeah, I've been wanting to battle Gekkouga again anyway.

05:57.350 --> 05:58.400
Now that that is decided...

05:59.830 --> 06:01.560
Rentorar, thank you for the hard work.

06:03.960 --> 06:05.090
I'll let them treat you too.

06:09.070 --> 06:10.000
Please put them here.

06:11.040 --> 06:12.040
Thank you.

06:12.040 --> 06:12.680
Thank you.

06:13.590 --> 06:14.750
Leave this to me.

06:18.000 --> 06:20.220
What should we do until the treatment is done?

06:21.140 --> 06:21.940
Let me think...

06:22.340 --> 06:25.550
Alan, do you have any other Pokémon besides Lizardon?

06:26.290 --> 06:27.870
I do, but...

06:28.620 --> 06:31.730
Then let's battle until Gekkouga recovers!

06:34.870 --> 06:35.620
Yeah, let's.

06:39.810 --> 06:41.580
Onvern, I choose you!

06:51.330 --> 06:54.390
Sorry, sorry. I wanted to let Onvern battle too.

06:56.850 --> 06:58.290
Onvern, do your best!

06:58.640 --> 06:59.510
Go for it!

07:00.050 --> 07:01.340
Go, Metang!

07:06.530 --> 07:07.390
A Metang, huh?

07:11.000 --> 07:14.640
Metang, the Iron Claw Pokémon. The evolved form of Dumbber.

07:15.070 --> 07:17.140
When two Dumbber fuse together, Metang is formed.

07:17.700 --> 07:20.860
The brains of the Dumbber are joined by a magnetic nervous system. By linking its brains magnetically,

07:20.860 --> 07:22.780
this Pokémon generates strong psychokinetic power.

07:23.740 --> 07:25.220
Metang is a Steel type.

07:25.840 --> 07:28.450
It is an opponent that Onvern, a Dragon type, has a disadvantage against.

07:28.790 --> 07:29.660
What?!

07:31.140 --> 07:32.340
Will they be all right?

07:33.780 --> 07:35.430
Let's take care of this, Onvern!

07:36.900 --> 07:37.660
Now then,

07:38.260 --> 07:38.690
start...

07:39.500 --> 07:40.150
...the battle!

07:45.700 --> 07:46.300
Let's go!

07:46.500 --> 07:47.180
Acrobatics!

07:52.160 --> 07:53.110
Metal Claw!

07:57.350 --> 07:58.390
Psyshock!

07:58.390 --> 07:58.980
Boomburst!

08:06.460 --> 08:07.570
Onvern isn't yielding an inch either!

08:08.060 --> 08:08.700
Supersonic!

08:14.180 --> 08:15.580
Supersonic hit its mark!

08:16.050 --> 08:17.290
Now, use Acrobatics!

08:18.690 --> 08:19.500
Psyshock!

08:29.950 --> 08:31.280
Meteor Mash!

08:34.070 --> 08:34.640
Dodge!

08:40.460 --> 08:41.270
Boomburst!

08:49.280 --> 08:50.110
Metal Claw!

08:50.420 --> 08:51.240
Acrobatics!

09:18.500 --> 09:19.900
Onvern is unable to battle!

09:20.470 --> 09:21.410
Alan wins!

09:23.920 --> 09:24.790
Onvern!

09:29.490 --> 09:32.800
You did well. This battle definitely won't have been a waste.

09:36.500 --> 09:39.580
Seeing how tough its opponent was, Onvern fought well.

09:39.580 --> 09:41.780
Yeah, it did really good!

09:43.790 --> 09:45.930
They almost got us.

09:51.720 --> 09:56.870
Satoshi-san, Citron-san. The Pokémon you left in my care have all recovered.

10:01.680 --> 10:02.680
Will this help you figure things out?

10:03.140 --> 10:06.570
My hypothesis is that the mysterious phenomenon that happens to Satoshi and Gekkouga is psychologically determined;

10:07.040 --> 10:12.070
or in other words, that the transformation might occur when their feelings synchronize.

10:13.480 --> 10:14.380
Synchronize, huh...?

10:14.820 --> 10:16.080
All ready here.

10:16.590 --> 10:17.750
I'm counting on you, Gekkouga.

10:28.160 --> 10:29.210
Go, Lizardon!

10:33.890 --> 10:35.220
All right, let us begin!

10:36.000 --> 10:37.470
Start the battle!

10:41.430 --> 10:42.690
We'll make the first move!

10:43.260 --> 10:43.980
Water Shuriken!

10:46.920 --> 10:47.940
Charge in, Lizardon!

10:48.290 --> 10:49.190
Dragon Claw!

11:05.830 --> 11:06.520
Pokémon Quiz.

11:07.170 --> 11:07.760
The answer is...?

11:10.550 --> 11:12.710
The Pokémon Elections 720!

11:13.590 --> 11:17.270
Push the d-button on your remote control and vote for the Pokémon you want!

11:17.980 --> 11:27.880
Coming up next:

11:17.980 --> 11:22.960
The battle gets even more intense!

11:18.900 --> 11:23.630
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

11:22.990 --> 11:27.880
Satoshi starts acting strange!?

11:36.540 --> 11:37.240
Double Team!

11:39.440 --> 11:40.350
Flamethrower!

11:40.560 --> 11:41.600
Mow them down!

11:50.130 --> 11:50.710
Cut!

12:00.520 --> 12:01.760
Good job, Gekkouga.

12:05.000 --> 12:08.690
Yeah, I agree. It really <i>is</i> more suitable to use this power against them.

12:09.630 --> 12:11.080
Respond to my heart,

12:11.330 --> 12:12.140
Key Stone!

12:12.390 --> 12:13.470
Surpass evolution!

12:13.800 --> 12:14.820
Mega evolve!

12:36.690 --> 12:37.270
Here it is.

12:38.470 --> 12:41.180
Now show me that alternate form of yours.

12:41.630 --> 12:43.020
Go! Thunder Punch!

12:45.390 --> 12:46.280
Aerial Ace!

12:56.930 --> 12:57.720
Amazing!

12:57.980 --> 12:59.280
Bro, how does it look?

13:00.290 --> 13:01.780
There are no changes in their battle pulses.

13:02.130 --> 13:03.080
Cut!

13:06.450 --> 13:06.710
Grab it!

13:10.270 --> 13:10.960
Flamethrower!

13:18.290 --> 13:19.280
Thunder Punch!

13:22.110 --> 13:22.890
Water Shuriken!

13:34.030 --> 13:35.650
Gekkouga, you can go on, right?

13:43.550 --> 13:44.580
That's the spirit.

13:57.360 --> 13:58.510
Their pulses...

13:59.890 --> 14:00.520
...are overlapping?

14:02.390 --> 14:04.600
Citron, what does that mean?

14:04.600 --> 14:06.060
The synchronization has started!

14:06.350 --> 14:08.820
We'll become much, much stronger!

14:09.270 --> 14:10.260
Let's go!

14:17.600 --> 14:18.320
They overlapped!

14:19.710 --> 14:20.360
It's starting!

14:20.620 --> 14:21.790
Go, go!

14:27.060 --> 14:29.240
So my hypothesis was correct after all!

14:29.700 --> 14:34.050
The transformation requires Satoshi and Gekkouga's feelings to synchronize!

14:34.460 --> 14:35.150
Let's go!

14:36.200 --> 14:36.990
Gekkouga!

14:44.700 --> 14:45.740
Cut!

14:48.500 --> 14:48.810
Here it comes!

14:50.890 --> 14:51.490
Dodge!

14:55.170 --> 14:56.030
Flamethrower!

15:00.240 --> 15:01.400
Cut!

15:03.780 --> 15:05.320
Go! Aerial Ace!

15:05.630 --> 15:06.480
Counter it!

15:06.790 --> 15:07.910
Thunder Punch!

15:16.230 --> 15:17.200
Go!

15:24.710 --> 15:27.430
This is it... This is what I've been waiting for!

15:28.050 --> 15:31.300
Lizardon, can you feel their power as well?

15:33.710 --> 15:35.470
Let's blast through this, Gekkouga!

15:36.300 --> 15:37.170
Cut!

15:38.790 --> 15:39.740
Dragon Claw!

15:56.060 --> 15:57.160
Cut!

16:06.380 --> 16:06.910
Lizardon!

16:19.480 --> 16:20.290
What's going on?

16:22.990 --> 16:23.540
Huh?

16:23.810 --> 16:26.460
Satoshi and Gekkouga's battle pulses are dispersing!

16:28.200 --> 16:28.950
What does this mean?

16:30.930 --> 16:32.150
What's going on?

16:34.160 --> 16:34.920
I can't move...

16:36.760 --> 16:37.440
What is this?

16:39.670 --> 16:40.350
What...

16:47.110 --> 16:47.710
Satoshi!

16:49.110 --> 16:50.070
What is the matter?!

16:57.180 --> 16:58.050
Satoshi!

16:58.230 --> 16:59.340
Satoshi!

17:06.290 --> 17:07.020
Gekkouga?

17:08.240 --> 17:10.200
What happened to us?

17:12.940 --> 17:14.560
My body won't move...

17:15.200 --> 17:16.040
Wait!

17:16.530 --> 17:17.720
Please wait, Gekkouga!

17:18.560 --> 17:19.340
Gekkouga!

17:22.540 --> 17:23.620
He's waking up!

17:23.620 --> 17:24.340
Satoshi!

17:25.150 --> 17:25.840
Are you all right?

17:26.400 --> 17:27.580
Uh, yeah...

17:31.180 --> 17:33.630
Thank goodness. You had us worried!

17:34.270 --> 17:35.550
Sorry, sorry.

17:35.550 --> 17:37.460
Take it easy for today, and get some rest.

17:37.830 --> 17:38.080
I will.

17:38.750 --> 17:40.310
Sorry it had to happen right in the middle of the battle.

17:41.190 --> 17:41.880
Don't worry about it.

17:42.630 --> 17:43.240
I...

17:44.620 --> 17:46.140
My body stopped moving...

17:47.730 --> 17:51.360
That just proves how much of a burden the synchronization places on the Trainer.

17:52.340 --> 17:53.870
That only makes sense.

17:54.690 --> 17:57.960
This power itself is unusual; I've never seen anything like it.

18:03.100 --> 18:05.170
Why did my body stop moving?

18:07.500 --> 18:07.990
Alan!

18:08.420 --> 18:11.380
Once we make this power ours, let's battle again!

18:11.940 --> 18:12.750
You're right,

18:13.800 --> 18:15.850
we didn't finish today's battle, after all.

18:18.530 --> 18:20.020
I'll become stronger and stronger,

18:20.510 --> 18:22.540
defeat you and win the Kalos League!

18:23.950 --> 18:25.570
Aim to be a Pokémon Master!

18:26.160 --> 18:27.380
The Kalos League, huh?

18:27.710 --> 18:29.280
You're aiming for that too, right, Alan?

18:29.900 --> 18:30.290
No,

18:30.870 --> 18:31.610
not really...

18:32.590 --> 18:33.150
Why not?

18:34.140 --> 18:38.120
Lots of super strong Trainers and Pokémon are going to gather there!

18:38.990 --> 18:40.540
Just thinking about it gets me excited!

18:42.770 --> 18:43.920
That sounds fun.

18:52.840 --> 18:53.860
There's nothing unusual going on here.

18:54.560 --> 18:56.840
I'll continue with the Mega Evolution energy...

18:56.840 --> 18:57.360
Wait.

18:58.390 --> 19:00.610
We have this footage for you from Fleur-de-lis-sama.

19:03.060 --> 19:04.450
Alan, listen to this!

19:06.290 --> 19:08.980
You know, Hari-san's spikes moved the other day!

19:10.700 --> 19:11.950
It was only a little, but they did twitch!

19:13.060 --> 19:14.450
That's all I wanted to tell you.

19:15.920 --> 19:18.620
We're fine here. Alan, you do your best too!

19:21.390 --> 19:21.840
That's all.

19:22.770 --> 19:23.900
Continue with your mission.

19:26.760 --> 19:28.340
What do you think of your battles with Satoshi?

19:31.950 --> 19:35.230
Makes you remember the times we spent at the professor's place, huh?

19:36.860 --> 19:38.050
We should become stronger too.

19:39.920 --> 19:40.850
If we don't,

19:41.990 --> 19:43.740
we won't be able to protect what's important to us.

19:51.330 --> 19:52.650
I'll become Gekkouga!

19:53.120 --> 19:53.500
What?

19:55.440 --> 19:57.590
I meant that I have to become just as strong.

19:58.530 --> 20:01.060
Until now, I've always had my Pokémon become stronger.

20:02.020 --> 20:03.710
Now it's <i>my</i> turn to become stronger.

20:04.740 --> 20:06.370
I have to do this, no matter what!

20:06.830 --> 20:13.750
This "future of new greatness which no one has ever seen before" that Gojika-san was talking about... Let's go towards it together, Gekkouga!

20:14.880 --> 20:16.640
This way of thinking is so like you, Satoshi.

20:17.070 --> 20:18.480
I've gotta work on my stamina!

20:18.760 --> 20:20.060
I'll start with a marathon!

20:22.500 --> 20:23.640
And with that said, the other guys should also...

20:30.380 --> 20:32.220
All right, let's all go together!

20:33.580 --> 20:34.690
Wait a second!

20:34.690 --> 20:36.190
Bro, hurry! Hurry!

20:36.190 --> 20:39.260
You must be joking! W-Wait, please!

20:39.560 --> 20:42.340
Will Satoshi become Gekkouga?

20:42.940 --> 20:44.630
What will be the outcome of this training?

20:45.380 --> 20:46.790
With the Eisetsu Gym before his eyes,

20:47.510 --> 20:48.770
Satoshi's challenge is...

20:54.850 --> 20:57.500
Special news on the Pokémon movie!

20:57.900 --> 20:59.060
Hey, Electric Mouse!

20:59.740 --> 21:01.860
Ya can't trust humans!

21:02.110 --> 21:04.420
Volcanion is characterized by the arms on its back.

21:05.240 --> 21:06.290
Get blown away!

21:06.290 --> 21:08.290
Its arms can obviously launch moves,

21:08.290 --> 21:09.360
Let's charge in!

21:09.360 --> 21:11.120
but they also allow it to fly!

21:12.480 --> 21:18.120
On sale until Friday July 15th

21:12.880 --> 21:15.520
There are special pre-order tickets with which you can receive Volcanion,

21:15.520 --> 21:17.180
which also has a huge role in the movie itself!

21:17.550 --> 21:19.550
Everyone, make sure to get one!

21:18.290 --> 21:20.840
Premieres Saturday July 16th!

21:20.870 --> 21:25.850
Sunday April 24th at 8am!

21:21.690 --> 21:23.530
Pokénchiwa!

21:23.530 --> 21:25.070
Pokénchi goes to Kyoto!

21:28.190 --> 21:30.100
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.270 --> 21:31.380
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.450 --> 21:39.310
According to legend, if you hear children's voices in a certain forest, you'll get lost and never get out again.

21:40.360 --> 21:40.690
Listen.

21:41.400 --> 21:42.840
You can hear them right now, can't you...?

21:47.630 --> 21:50.170
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:50.610 --> 21:52.290
The Forest's Curse and the White Bokurei!

21:52.290 --> 21:55.780
Next Time

21:52.290 --> 21:55.780
The Forest's Curse and the White Bokurei!

21:53.240 --> 21:55.060
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:55.810 --> 22:05.850
Next episode:

21:55.810 --> 22:00.760
A Bokurei falls from the sky!

21:56.830 --> 22:01.400
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

22:00.800 --> 22:05.850
Let's become friends with Bokurei!
